WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.920
Speaker 1: Hello, everybody. Welcome to The David&nbsp;
Pakman Show. I'm producer Pat Forde, filling in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:09.120
once again for David today as he is traveling up&nbsp;
north in Canada. But fear not because David will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:14.240
be back with us at the end of the week. So let's&nbsp;
jump into some stories. Donald Trump is taking a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:19.680
huge political risk and demanding that the full,&nbsp;
unredacted affidavit that led to his search&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:25.280
of his Mar a Lago home get released to the public&nbsp;
because he believes that it's going to vindicate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:30.560
him. And the judge in the case, Bruce Rinehart,&nbsp;
actually may decide to call his bluff on this. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:35.440
affidavit, of course, was the evidence that was&nbsp;
used to convince Rinehart that there was probable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:40.240
cause to conduct the search warrant at Mar a&nbsp;
Lago. Trump's spokesperson, Taylor BORDEWICH,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:44.560
said about it, quote, President Trump has made&nbsp;
his view clear that the American people should&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:50.320
be permitted to see the unredacted affidavit&nbsp;
related to the raid and break in of his home. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:57.280
Trump himself made the same call on truth social&nbsp;
a.k.a. truth central posting. There is no way to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.280 --> 00:01:02.640
justify the unannounced raid of Mar a Lago, the&nbsp;
home of the 45th president of the United States,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:06.720
who got more votes, by the way, than any&nbsp;
sitting president in the history of our country.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:12.320
Not more votes than Joe Biden, by the way, by a&nbsp;
very large number of gun toting FBI agents and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.320 --> 00:01:18.160
the Department of Justice. But in the interests&nbsp;
of transparency, I call for the immediate release&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:23.440
of the completely unredacted affidavit pertaining&nbsp;
to this horrible and shocking break in. Also, the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:28.480
judge on the case should recuse. Now, what exactly&nbsp;
should Judge Bruce Reinhart recuse himself for?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:32.480
Nobody knows. And will Donald Trump ever&nbsp;
articulate why he should recuse himself?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:36.640
Probably not. But it's just something you throw&nbsp;
out there, I guess. Judge Reinhart is actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:40.960
open to the idea of releasing the affidavit&nbsp;
with some of the appropriate redactions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:45.600
included the specifics of which are going&nbsp;
to be recommended to him by next Thursday.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:49.440
But the Trump team, it's not good enough for&nbsp;
them. They want the full affidavit without&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:54.080
any redactions released to the public, which&nbsp;
really should be no surprise to us all, because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:59.120
clearly Trump and his team are not too careful&nbsp;
about how they handle sensitive information,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.120 --> 00:02:03.200
which is exactly why he's in this mess to begin&nbsp;
with. Right? That's exactly why he decided to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:07.520
bring those documents with him down to Mar a&nbsp;
Lago and put them in the basement. Redactions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:12.400
would probably include cutting out some of the&nbsp;
names of the people involved in the investigation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:17.120
of the former presidents. And they're totally&nbsp;
fine at the Trump team just saying, oh, don't,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:21.600
don't cut out those names. Don't cut out the very&nbsp;
classified stuff that you don't want released to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:27.200
the public because we don't care if people get&nbsp;
put in harm's way over this. Now, the call to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:32.160
release the affidavit does seem to be a little&nbsp;
bit risky to Trump because it could reveal the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:36.880
communications between the Trump team and the&nbsp;
DOJ ahead of the raid, which is when they asked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:41.920
him for specific documents. And if this comes out,&nbsp;
this could totally debunk the claim that Trump has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.920 --> 00:02:46.720
been making, that he had this great relationship&nbsp;
with the DOJ and he was cooperating fully. Thus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:51.920
the raid was totally unnecessary. It could also&nbsp;
just provide further evidence of how exactly Trump&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:57.120
was mishandling classified information, which&nbsp;
again is not a good look for him. It seems like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.120 --> 00:03:02.000
the potential upside to Trump, though, is that if&nbsp;
the judge decides not to release the affidavit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:07.200
that's going to help him, because Trump could&nbsp;
say, Oh, look, they're not even being willing to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:10.720
release all of the information.&nbsp;
They're not telling us why they're&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.720 --> 00:03:15.680
investigating me. This is a witch hunt. They're&nbsp;
trying to keep everything secret. By the way,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.680 --> 00:03:19.440
it's not common for affidavits to get released to&nbsp;
the public. They're just considering it in this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:23.840
case because of the public interest. So maybe the&nbsp;
Trump team, not that they make this ask knowing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:28.480
that it wasn't going to be granted to them, but&nbsp;
Bruce Rinehart seemingly willing to call his bluff&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:34.000
and this could end up backfiring tremendously&nbsp;
on Trump and his team. So this is very much part&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:39.200
of the throw everything at the wall and see what&nbsp;
sticks strategy. Let's talk more about that next.

